  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Bell Boeing Joint Project Office obligated $1.1B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Bell Boeing Joint Project Office received 1,058 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1000K. Bell Boeing Joint Project Office obligations are down 21.7% year over year. Bell Boeing Joint Project Office gets nearly all buying from the Department of Defense, which obligated $1.1B, with the General Services Administration obligating $2.1M. Bell Boeing Joint Project Office sells primarily aircraft-related goods and services: Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing leads with $682M and Aircraft Manufacturing follows with $333M. Bell Boeing Joint Project Office also shows $35.2M in Computer Systems Design Services, $5.1M in Other Metal Valve and Pipe Fitting Manufacturing, $2.1M in Engineering Services, and $0 in Machine Tool Manufacturing. Bell Boeing Joint Project Office fiscal-year history shows obligations of $2.5B in FY21, $1.9B in FY22, $947M in FY23, $871M in FY24, $1.4B in FY25, and $1.1B in FY26 to date. The current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity.",
    "sections": [
